{
  "finalText": "The deploy failed because migration 0042 timed out building an index on `events.user_id`, and that table has no index in prod. Prod never got it because migration 0041 was manually marked as applied in 2024 without actually running — so the index it was supposed to create never existed, and 0042 tried to build it against a full unindexed table and blew the timeout. Staging has the index, which is why it only broke in prod.\n\nFix is to reconcile the migration state: build the index on `events.user_id` in prod (concurrently, off-hours), then confirm 0041/0042 both register as genuinely applied before the next deploy.\n\nTwo things I noticed but didn't touch: a couple of flaky tests, and three theories I ruled out (OOM, bad env var, stale docker cache) in case they come up. Say the word if you want me to handle the index or dig into the flakies.",
